## Escalation Checklist

Escalate to L2/L3 if any of the following apply:

- [ ] Conditional Access policy is blocking all users — check the **Sign-in logs** in Entra before touching the policy
- [ ] MFA reset completed but user still can't sign in — may be a token/session issue; escalate with sign-in log export
- [ ] Device stuck in **"Pending"** compliance state for more than 30 minutes — possible MDM enrollment issue
- [ ] Wipe or retire action fails or does not reach the device — device may be offline; document the attempt with a timestamp
- [ ] User reports being blocked despite the device showing Compliant — Conditional Access evaluation issue; pull sign-in logs
- [ ] Licence assignment fails with a "no licences available" error — L2 to review licence pool with billing

```powershell
# Useful diagnostics to gather before escalating

# Export sign-in logs for a specific user (last 24 hours)
Connect-MgGraph -Scopes "AuditLog.Read.All"
Get-MgAuditLogSignIn -Filter "userPrincipalName eq 'jane.doe@labintune.onmicrosoft.com'" `
  -Top 20 |
  Select CreatedDateTime, AppDisplayName, ConditionalAccessStatus, Status |
  Format-Table -AutoSize

# Check available licences remaining
Get-MgSubscribedSku |
  Select SkuPartNumber,
    @{N="Assigned"; E={$_.ConsumedUnits}},
    @{N="Total";    E={$_.PrepaidUnits.Enabled}} |
  Format-Table -AutoSize

# Get full device details for escalation
Get-MgDeviceManagementManagedDevice -Filter "deviceName eq 'CLIENT01'" |
  Select DeviceName, SerialNumber, EnrolledDateTime, LastSyncDateTime,
         ComplianceState, OperatingSystem, OsVersion, UserPrincipalName
```

